# Mosquitto ACL — mqtt.offx1.com (authoritative, 2026-09-25)
# Pasted by John from the broker's acl_file. Verbatim record.

# ============ muse user (bridge subscriber + Muse agent) ============
user muse
# Bridge reads page telemetry, status, audio
topic read watcher/telemetry
topic read watcher/status
topic read watcher/audio
# Bridge publishes status here; also receives console pings
topic readwrite watcher/bridge
# Muse agent sends device commands (bridge does not need to read these)
topic write watcher/command
# Bridge monitors keepalive and jiggler state (page publishes)
topic read watcher/keepalive
topic read watcher/jiggle
# Muse driving state: agent publishes, bridge monitors
topic readwrite watcher/muse
# Pause state: bidirectional (page publishes pill clicks, agent publishes remote pause)
topic readwrite watcher/muse_pause
# Command queue: bidirectional (page publishes depth, agent can clear)
topic readwrite watcher/muse_queue
# Heartbeats: bridge listens (added 2026-09-25; no consumer in subscriber.py yet)
topic read watcher/heartbeat
topic read watcher/console_heartbeat

# ============ watcher user (console page) ============
user watcher
# Page publishes telemetry and status to the bridge
topic write watcher/telemetry
topic write watcher/status
# Bridge status and ping: page receives status, sends pings
topic readwrite watcher/bridge
# Device commands: page receives from agent only
topic read watcher/command
# Keepalive and jiggler: page publishes config, receives remote state
topic readwrite watcher/keepalive
topic readwrite watcher/jiggle
# Muse driving state: page receives only
topic read watcher/muse
# Pause state: bidirectional
topic readwrite watcher/muse_pause
# Command queue: bidirectional
topic readwrite watcher/muse_queue

# ---- Auditor notes (Muse, 2026-09-25) ----
# 1. No ACL entry for watcher/heartbeat or watcher/console_heartbeat,
#    yet the console publishes to both (forwardDeviceHeartbeat,
#    mqttConsoleHeartbeat). Mosquitto default-denies unmatched topics
#    when acl_file is set -> these publishes are silently dropped.
#    Either add `topic write watcher/heartbeat` (+ console_heartbeat)
#    for the watcher user, or stop publishing them.
# 2. No user has write on watcher/audio (muse: read; watcher: none).
#    The page currently batches audio chunks into watcher/telemetry
#    instead; watcher/audio is aspirational ("preferred once the
#    console routes t:audio here" per subscriber.py).
# 3. muse has read-only on watcher/jiggle and watcher/keepalive:
#    remote jiggler/keepalive control must go through watcher/command
#    (sealed), never direct topic writes. Matches the 2026-09-24
#    silent-drop finding.
# 4. 2026-09-26: an ACL-vs-topics checker now guards every publish
#    (topic_acl.py + audit_topics.py, John's go-ahead). Runtime: all bridge
#    publish paths go through publish_checked(), which blocks topics the ACL
#    doesn't grant with a loud ACL-DENY banner instead of letting the broker
#    silently drop them. One-shot scripts raise (non-zero exit); daemons
#    (subscriber.py bridge_publish, keepalive.py _pub) log-and-skip so the
#    bridge never dies over a bad topic. Static: audit_topics.py checks
#    every bridge publish site (AST) + every page mqttPublish site (parsed
#    from watcher-console.html) against this file; run it before shipping
#    any bridge/console patch and after any broker ACL change (re-mirror
#    this file first). Live violations it currently flags: keepalive.py's
#    retained publishes to watcher/keepalive + watcher/jiggle as muse
#    (read-only for muse -- silently dropped today), jiggle.py ditto, and
#    the page's watcher/heartbeat + watcher/console_heartbeat as watcher
#    (still ungranted -- see note 1).
